   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recovery and resilience building for Vulnerable households affected by climatic and environmental shocks in the Grand Sud of Madagascar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will build on previous interventions and enter into this wider dynamic aiming at improving the resilience of households livelihoods in the districts of Ampanihy and Betioky Atsimo. It will focus on (i) the diversification of sources of food and income for vulnerable households and improving market access for their local products, (ii) the capacity building of farmers on climate-smart agriculture (CSA) to increase and stabilize production, increase adaptation and mitigation of producers to risks; linked to climate change and natural hazards and sustainable management and use of natural resources and (iii) the capacity building of households on nutrition-sensitive agriculture (NSA) associated with food diversification, best practices for food processing/ preservation/ preparation.</narrative>
  </description>
